# ----- .claude: track the research pipeline, ignore machine-specific state -----
# Ported from github.com/hugosantanna/clo-author (2026-07-16). Agents, skills,
# rules and references are the shared system and belong in git so they reach the Mac.
# settings.local.json and state/ stay local: machine paths and session guards.
#
# NOTE: this must be `.claude/*`, not `.claude/`. Git does not descend into an
# excluded *directory*, so `!` negations under it never get evaluated. That is why
# commands/pull-paper.md sat uncommitted for months under the old `.claude/` rule.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/references/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/scripts/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/WORKFLOW_QUICK_REF.md
.vscode/
*.log

# ----- macOS / R session noise -----
.DS_Store
*.Rhistory

# ----- Graphs/maps: shapefiles + oversized map PDF exceed GitHub 100MB limit -----
Graphs/maps/shapefiles/
Graphs/maps/sample_geography_map.pdf

# ----- Reference papers (copyrighted; not part of research code) -----
Programs/entry_exit/Lagos JMP (2026).pdf

# ----- OpenAI Codex CLI (not part of research) -----
.codex
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# ----- Submodules (not part of research repo) -----
Resume
markitdown

# ----- layer_connectivity_standalone: ignore data, keep scripts -----
layer_connectivity_standalone/data/
__pycache__/

# ----- Data files (too large for git) -----
